 By Neil Irwin and Courtenay Brown &middot; Oct 01, 2026 
 
 
 Major economies may be chafing at the Trump administration's sweeping tariffs on imports, but some of the logic behind them is being more widely embraced.

 More below, from the sidelines of a G20 trade ministers meeting in Milwaukee. Plus, a new seven-layer metaphor for inflationary pressures in the economy. Today's newsletter, edited by George Moriarty and copy edited by Amy Stern, is 1,012 words, a 4-minute read. 

 
 
